<p><img src="https://cdn3.brettterpstra.com/uploads/2026/11/nvalt-highlight-rb.7542.jpg" width="800" height="226" style="margin:0 auto;clear:both;" class="header" /></p>
<p>nvALT 3.0.36 is out, and the stretch from 3.0.32 to here is mostly the editor catching up with the way I actually write notes. Highlights show up while I type, CriticMarkup is readable without opening Preview, and a pile of small window bugs stopped getting in the way.</p>

<h3 id="highlights-in-the-editor">Highlights in the editor</h3>

<p><img src="https://cdn3.brettterpstra.com/uploads/2026/11/nvalt-highlight-screenshot-800.jpg"></p>

<p>Preview already turned <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">==highlight==</code> into a yellow mark. The editor ignored it, including a <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">highlight</code> entry in a theme. It colors that syntax now.</p>

<div class="language-markdown highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight fixed"><code>Ship the ==search highlight== fix before the blog post.</code></pre></div></div>

<p>If the theme defines <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">highlight</code>, that color wins. If it doesn&rsquo;t, the words are black on yellow. The <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">==</code> marks stay in the markup color, same idea as the asterisks around bold.</p>

<p>Select some text and press <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">=</code> and the selection becomes <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">==selection==</code>. Press <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">~</code> and it becomes <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">~~selection~~</code>. Neither key inserts a pair when nothing is selected. A lone <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">=</code> is still just an equals sign.</p>

<h3 id="criticmarkup">CriticMarkup</h3>

<p>The five CriticMarkup marks are colored in the editor too.</p>

<div class="language-markdown highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight fixed"><code>{++Add this sentence.++}
{--Cut this one.--}
{~~awkward~&gt;clearer~~}
{==Come back to this.==}
{&gt;&gt;Remember why this paragraph exists.&lt;&lt;}</code></pre></div></div>

<p>Deletions are red and crossed out. Insertions are green and underlined. A substitution shows the old half crossed out and the new half underlined. Highlights are yellow. Comments are cyan.</p>

<p>Those are the defaults. A theme that already has <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">criticAddition</code>, <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">criticDeletion</code>, <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">criticSubstitution</code>, <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">criticHighlight</code>, or <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">criticComment</code> uses those colors instead. Svelte&rsquo;s gold highlight stays gold. The underline and the strikethrough stay put either way, because that&rsquo;s what the marks mean.</p>

<p>Marks inside code are left alone, same as Preview.</p>

<h3 id="search-highlights-that-survive-a-dark-theme">Search highlights that survive a dark theme</h3>

<p>Search highlighting had a bad run on dark themes. A translucent highlight was mixed onto the old paper-white background, so on Svelte it turned into a gray bar. The matched letters were then drawn in black, which disappeared into the note.</p>

<p>The highlight is mixed onto the theme&rsquo;s editor background now. Opaque colors stay as you set them. When a match stops matching, those letters go back to the theme color instead of staying black.</p>

<p>The marks also stick around while I move through the notes the search found. They clear when the editor takes focus, and when the search field is emptied. The notes list still doesn&rsquo;t paint the search words into titles. This is the note body.</p>

<h3 id="scroll-bars-sharing-and-the-preview">Scroll bars, sharing, and the preview</h3>

<p>The notes list, the editor, and the preview use the system scroll bars. The old &ldquo;Use nvALT Scrollbars&rdquo; setting is gone, and scrolling no longer leaves extra knobs behind.</p>

<p>The preview stays on the block I&rsquo;m editing. It only scrolls when that block leaves the screen, so typing doesn&rsquo;t yank the preview back to the top.</p>

<p>There&rsquo;s a Share button in the title bar. It sends the selection, or the whole note when nothing is selected. Share Preview sends the rendered note as rich text, which is the one I want when pasting into another notes app. Open in Marked is no longer its own toolbar button. Share to Marked from that menu instead. View Source is a <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">&lt;/&gt;</code> icon, with the sync toggle beside it.</p>

<h3 id="the-window-stopped-fighting-the-search-field">The window stopped fighting the search field</h3>

<p>Tiling the window, or making it very narrow, used to leave the search field hanging off the edge or stuck at the width the window had when it opened. It follows the window now, in both layouts. In side-by-side layout it starts just after the title, the same way it does in vertical layout. The Share button stays on the right edge as the window grows.</p>

<p>Moving the selection no longer leaves a hairline on a fractional line. Tab and Backtab on a task checkbox indent the item instead of dropping in link brackets.</p>

<p>These are mostly quality of life fixes, thanks for all the reports and feature requests. And a special thanks to those who have shown their appreciation with a small donation.</p>

